The module performs network I/O at import time (fetches a secret and opens a DB connection). Every import — including test collection — pays that cost and needs AWS access; a failure makes the module unimportable. Move the side effects into functions, create them lazily and cache:

```python
import functools, json

@functools.cache
def get_conn():
    import boto3, psycopg2
    secret = json.loads(boto3.client("secretsmanager")
                        .get_secret_value(SecretId="prod/db")["SecretString"])
    return psycopg2.connect(**secret)

def fetch_jobs(conn=None):
    conn = conn or get_conn()
    with conn.cursor() as cur:
        cur.execute("SELECT id FROM jobs")
        return cur.fetchall()
```

Tests can now pass their own connection.
